**`CoachScreen.loadProfile()` — sequential waterfall** (`mobile/src/screens/CoachScreen.tsx:276`)

Three parallel queries run first, then two *sequential* queries fire after — one for free users' message count, one for habit completions. That's 5 round trips where 3 is the minimum:

```ts
// Current: 3 parallel → then 2 sequential (worst case 3 round trips)
const [userData, habitsData, checkinRows] = await Promise.all([...]);

// Sequential #1 — only for free users
const { count } = await supabase.from('chat_messages')...
// Sequential #2 — needs habit IDs from habitsData
const { data: completions } = await supabase.from('habit_completions')...
```

Fix: include `chat_messages` count in the initial `Promise.all` and keep the completions query parallel too — habit IDs are available before the await resolves:

```ts
const today = new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0];
const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser();

// Kick off ALL queries at once
const completionsPromise = supabase.from('habit_completions').select('habit_id')
  .eq('date', today); // we'll filter by user_id via RLS, or join

const [userData, habitsData, checkinRows, msgCount] = await Promise.all([
  supabase.from('users').select('...').eq('id', user.id).single(),
  supabase.from('habits').select('id').eq('user_id', user.id),
  supabase.from('check_ins').select('type, mission').eq('user_id', user.id).eq('date', today),
  supabase.from('chat_messages')
    .select('*', { count: 'exact', head: true })
    .eq('user_id', user.id).eq('role', 'user').gte('created_at', today),
]);
// then filter completions client-side using habitsData
```

---

**`buildCoachContext()` — habits → completions waterfall** (`mobile/src/services/context.ts:46`)

```ts
// Current: 4 parallel, then sequential completions fetch
const [userResult, habitsResult, goalsResult, checkinResult] = await Promise.all([...]);
// ...
if (habitIds.length > 0) {
  const { data: completions } = await supabase  // ← extra round trip
    .from('habit_completions').select('habit_id').eq('date', today).in('habit_id', habitIds);
}
```

This function is called on **every message send** and **every pep talk** — meaning users pay this round-trip cost 5+ times per session. Fix with a DB view or RPC that joins habits + completions in one query, or cache the result for ~60s:

```ts
// Option A: single RPC
const { data } = await supabase.rpc('get_coach_context', { p_user_id: userId });

// Option B: module-level cache (simple, good enough)
const contextCache = new Map<string, { data: CoachContext; ts: number }>();

export async function buildCoachContext(userId: string): Promise<CoachContext> {
  const cached = contextCache.get(userId);
  if (cached && Date.now() - cached.ts < 60_000) return cached.data;
  // ... fetch ...
  contextCache.set(userId, { data: ctx, ts: Date.now() });
  return ctx;
}
```

